# Sveltia site

SvelteKit static site with Git-based [Sveltia CMS](https://sveltiacms.app/en/). Independent from the Python `web/` generator — uses its own data copy under `sveltia/src/lib/`.

## Do not confuse with the Python pipeline

| Python pipeline | Sveltia site |
|-----------------|--------------|
| `data/structured/*.json` arrays | `sveltia/src/lib/data/{course-types,courses,venues,people,testimonials}/*.json` (one file per entry) |
| `scripts/build_web.py` → `web/` | SvelteKit routes → `sveltia/build/` |
| Edit rendering in `build_web.py` | Edit Svelte components and `sveltia/src/app.css` |

Optional sync: `cd sveltia && npm run sync-data` reads `../data/` and overwrites synced paths. Course types are not synced; listing `course` relations are preserved.

## Data loading

- JSON: `import.meta.glob` in `sveltia/src/lib/data.ts`
- Markdown: `import.meta.glob` in `sveltia/src/lib/markdown.ts`
- Public URL slug = last segment of listing `id`
- Dated listings (`courses/*.json`) may set `course` to a course-type `id`. `resolveListing()` in `src/lib/courses.ts` fills blank inheritable fields from the course type.

## CMS (`sveltia/static/admin/config.yml`)

- **Folder collections:** course-types, courses, venues, people, testimonials (one JSON file each)
- **File collection:** pages (single Markdown files)
- **Folder collection:** articles
- CMS repo root = nosetonose git root (not `sveltia/` alone)
- Listings link to course types, venues, and people via relation widgets (`id` fields)
- The **Courses** tab is dated listings (events). **Course types** are date-agnostic programmes.
- Course `schedule`, `course_description`, and `accommodation_and_meals` are `text` widgets, not `markdown`. Lexical cannot parse scraped copy and a thrown editor blanks every field. The public site still renders those strings as Markdown.
- Unused single relations (`course`, `venue`) must **omit the key**. JSON `null` or `""` blanks the CMS entry editor. `output.omit_empty_optional_fields` in `config.yml` stops the CMS writing them back as `null`.
- Empty Markdown-ish text fields must be `""` (not `null`).
- JSON files keep `id` as the first key. CMS field order starts with ID so a save does not shuffle it.

## Page composition gotchas

**Home (`/`):** Only “About us” (`home-team.md`) and testimonials are fully CMS-driven. Approach section is an excerpt of `approach.md` (until `# What happens in a workshop`). Hero and newsletter UI are in `+page.svelte`; newsletter URL in `src/lib/home.ts`.

**Courses index:** Grouped by region, then clown level, then course type title (or listing title if unlinked), then date. Sidebar lists regions and nested levels.

**Course detail:** Merged listing + venue. Facilitator block shows photo + first paragraph of `background` via `firstParagraph()` in `src/lib/people.ts`.

**Team:** Intro paragraph is hardcoded in `team/+page.svelte`; people lists come from JSON. Person course lists use merged facilitator ids.

**Not synced by `sync-data.py`:** `home-team.md`, `course-types/` — edit in CMS or directly.

## Where to edit

| Goal | Edit |
|------|------|
| Course type / listing / venue / person / testimonial fields | CMS or `sveltia/src/lib/data/*/` |
| Editorial page copy | CMS or `sveltia/src/lib/content/pages/` |
| Layout, routes, derived page logic | `sveltia/src/routes/`, `sveltia/src/lib/` |
| CMS collections/fields | `sveltia/static/admin/config.yml` |
| Refresh from scrape pipeline | `sveltia/scripts/sync-data.py` |

